                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I played this on the Oculus Rift with Touch controllers and can confirm it is NOW Oculus compatible (at least on the beta version).\n\nI did purchase this game originally.  But the Touch controllers did not work at all.  I requested and got a full refund.  I wrote a review complaining about the lack of Oculus Rift comptability.  The dev responded by saying he would work on that and sent me a key in exchange for testing the beta build.  \n\nI really worked for this key.  Looking back at it, I would rather have paid.  Time is money.  However, in the end, I am very happy to have been a part of the Oculus Rift compatibility of this game.  For whatever reason, there aren't too many open world exploration games in VR.  I would describe this game as a meditative exploration game with very light puzzle and shooter elements.  The puzzles are logical (not find a hidden key type of puzzle).\n\nThe graphics are cute and cartoony.  The world is imaginative.  It is not the biggest VR world so don't expect to explore for hours on end.  In fact, the game from start to finish for the average gamer will probably be 30-40 minutes.  For experienced gamers, it may be as little as 15 minutes.  A very casual gamer may take an hour or longer.    \n\nMovement is by teleportation.  You can choose blink or slide.  I prefer slide.  I think this game is meant to be taken in slowly.  It's more about enjoying the world versus trying to speedrun.  Unfortunately, the game does end suddenly at the final boss.  The final boss fight was anti-climatic.  That's really my main criticism.  This needed more difficulty, whether there's a hidden weakness to boss or a more intense encounter.  \n\nI do recommend this game.  I probably spent more than $4.99 timewise on this game playtesting it.  But I enjoyed the final product.  And I am happy to have been a part of it.  Now go exploring!",
                        "timestamp_created": 1511747114,
                        "timestamp_updated": 1513534216,
                        "voted_up": true,
                        "votes_up": 4,
                        "votes_funny": 0,
                        "weighted_vote_score": 0.5868245959281921,
                        "comment_count": 1,
                        "steam_purchase": false,
                        "received_for_free": true,
                        "written_during_early_access": false,
                        "developer_response": "Edit: The below response was to this user's original review.\n\nHi, I'm sorry that you were unable to play the game. Yes, the game currently only supports the HTC Vive wands for input. When this game was released, the Oculus Touch had just been made available and was sold out. Since I had started development before the Oculus Touch came out, the input system I used was specific to HTC Vive. OpenVR did not yet support Oculus Touch! I did not intentionally block Oculus users.\n\n\tThe reason I did not add Touch support later on is that, frankly, the game did not sell very well. I didn't think there would be sufficient interest. I decided instead to focus on a new project. But, well, now I can see someone is interested! I will start work on adding Oculus Touch support. I should (probably) be done before the weekend. If you are still interested in playing the game, let me know, and I can send you a key :)",
                        "timestamp_dev_responded": 1513539631,
